<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see sun west, some rain east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see sun west, some rain east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Tuesday were forecast to see sun in the west, some rain in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 21 to 24 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see mainly sunny skies with showers in the northeast and highs of 19 to 25 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see a few showers with highs of 14 to 19 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
